cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fevm-replay or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "fevm-replay: Ethereum mainnet replayed and validated statelessly in fevm, the EVM written in Fe"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mantoro"
    given-names: "Pugar Huda"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PugarHuda/fevm-replay"
url: "https://fevm-replay.vercel.app"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.8.6
date-released: "2026-11-23"
keywords:
  - Ethereum
  - Fe
  - EVM
  - stateless validation
  - EIP-4762
  - Glamsterdam
  - light client
abstract: >-
  Replays real Ethereum mainnet transactions in fevm, the EVM written in Fe,
  validates whole mainnet blocks statelessly from the parent's Merkle proofs
  (every root in the header), in a browser too, and measures what EIP-4762 and
  Glamsterdam's execution rules would do to today's transactions.
